title: log panel
tags: Panel [[Event log]]
kind: reference
summary: The repository's history as a tree of labels — a unit of work per row (a command, a script's run, the watcher's flushes folded), opening down to single operations, with badges saying what each is.

Open it with `panel:open here log` (<<key "panel:open here log" "t o">>). One row per
''unit of work'', newest first by its newest operation: for what you wrote, the outermost
label it was written in — a command, a script's run, a context you opened ([[Labels and contexts]]) —; for the watcher, one flush. Consecutive flushes of the watcher fold into a
single row (`N flushes of the watcher`), or they would drown the rest. A row opens onto
the labels nested in it and its own operations, newest first, down to single operations:
a run onto its answers, an answer onto its commands, a command onto what it wrote.

A label row shows its number, name and description, the time of its newest operation,
how many operations of the window are under it, and ''status'' badges — what decides
whether undoing it makes sense, computed over everything under it:

* `HEAD` — the newest operation is under it;
* `watcher` — the daemon wrote it for the filesystem ([[Operations and their origin]]); the row is dimmed, and `log:undo` skips it;
* `undo of #N` — it reverts what label `#N` wrote;
* `undone by #N` (or `partly undone`) — a later revert still standing took it back; a row fully undone is struck through, and reverting it again says so first.

!! Moving around

* <<key "log:next" "↓ or j">> / <<key "log:prev" "↑ or k">>, <<key "log:first" Home>> / <<key "log:last" End>>, <<key "log:find" f>> (a row on screen by label number or name, [[Jumping to an entry]]) — the selection, over every listed row.
* <<key "log:toggle ops" Enter>> (or a double click) — open the row under the cursor, and close it. The cursor then walks what it holds too, and a revert aims at what is under it: a label whole — what is nested in it included —, or one operation.
* <<key "log:toggle watcher" Shift+w>> — hide or show the watcher's work (shown by default). A display filter over what was fetched; the status line says how many units are hidden, and a selection inside one is dropped.
* ''Show older operations'' — the list fetches the newest thousand operations, so a repository with millions of them still opens; the button widens the window by as much again.
* <<key "log:refresh" r>> — read the log again. The status line gives how many units of work and operations are listed, and the repository's totals when the window is only part of the log.

!! Acting

<<key "log:revert" Shift+r>>, <<key "log:revert op" Shift+o>>, <<key "log:revert label" Shift+v>>,
`log:prune` — and the global <<key "log:undo" Ctrl+z>> / <<key "log:redo" Ctrl+Shift+z>>,
also as toolbar buttons: [[Log commands in the GUI]].

The cursor is published as `selected_log_entry`, which the [[log-detail panel]] follows.
